In our case, the ratio of a (AB) to c (AC) is the same as the ratio of b (BC) to c (DE). Hence, we can write (a/c) = (b/c), which can be rearranged to c^2 = a^2 + b^2. This demonstrates the Pythagorean theorem geometrically.[0m
