6. Harvesting: When the culture reaches high density, gently filter or centrifuge the dinoflagellates to separate them from the culture medium. Minimize exposure to light and maintain a cool temperature during harvesting to preserve bioluminescence.
7. Storage: Store harvested dinoflagellates in a cool, dark environment, such as a refrigerator, to preserve their bioluminescence.[0m
